# Intent: Dice Poker's screen drawn by ONE draw callback instead of 36 LVGL objects (owner request after docs/plan/games-visual-budget.md: every LVGL object is internal RAM, and 36 of them is about 4.6 KB of the 15.8 KB worst-case headroom). The dice, the pips, the buttons and every word are drawn inside one object like the board games; the screen keeps its call (dpk::screen(parent, state, es)) and its look, owns a copy of the state and frees it with the object. Two LVGL objects with the root.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_dicepoker.h (ours, patch UX18)
# Check after a flash: Dice Poker looks as before (dice with pips, HOLD under a held die, the hand's name, Roll again and Keep); a game of five rounds plays through; internal free during the game is about 4 KB higher than with UX18 alone.
# Kconfig: none

diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/maipai_dicepoker.h b/firmware/main/hal/maipai_dicepoker.h
--- a/firmware/main/hal/maipai_dicepoker.h
